---
/** `/privacy/`: what the site keeps about event guests and how they control it. STATIC. */
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import {staticContext} from '../../server/page';

export const prerender = true;

const {site, viewer} = await staticContext(Astro.request);
---

<Base site={site} viewer={viewer} isStatic title="Privacy" description="What we keep when you RSVP to an event, why, for how long, and how to download, correct or erase it.">
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="wrap narrow section">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What we keep</h2>
      <p>
        When you RSVP we keep your name, your email, your answer, any answers to the host's questions, and your ticket and check-in
        status. If you buy a ticket we keep the amount and its status, never your card details. If you tick the updates box we keep
        that choice.
      </p>
      <h2>Updates from the host</h2>
      <p>
        Updates are off unless you tick the box when you RSVP, and they only start once you click "Yes, send me updates" in the email
        we send you. Every update has an unsubscribe link, and it takes one click.
      </p>
      <h2>Your link</h2>
      <p>
        The email confirming your RSVP has a private link to manage your RSVP and your data. Anyone with the link can use it, so do
        not forward it. If you lose it, ask for a new one on the event page; the old one stops working.
      </p>
      <h2>Download or erase your data</h2>
      <p>
        From your private link you can download everything we hold about you for that event as a JSON file, or erase it. Erasing
        removes your name, email and answers and frees your seat. Payment records stay, without your name.
      </p>
      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Guest details are removed two years after the event ends. The download link works for 180 days after the event; erasing and
        unsubscribing always work.
      </p>
      <h2>Visits</h2>
      <p>
        We count event page visits with a salted hash that changes every day, so a visit cannot be tied to you or followed from one
        day to the next. We do not store your IP address.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
